.TH SYSLOGNG2RSYSLOG 1 "2026-11" "syslogd-rs 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
syslogng2rsyslog \- convert common syslog-ng configuration to rsyslog subset
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B syslogng2rsyslog
.RI < input.conf
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B syslogng2rsyslog
reads a syslog-ng configuration on standard input and emits the
supported rsyslog subset on standard output: sources (udp/tcp/
unix-dgram), destinations (file/udp/tcp), simple filters
(facility/level), and log paths, with
.B flags(final)
mapped to
.B stop.
Unconvertible constructs are reported as
.B "line N: unsupported construct"
and produce a non-zero exit status (fail-closed, same policy as
the daemon parser). It is intended for one-shot migration, not
continuous fidelity.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR syslogd-rs (8),
.BR rsyslog.conf (5)
